      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In the Utah climate, a roof lasts anywhere from 15 to 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, while premium materials like metal, tile, or slate can last 40 to 100+ years.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "15 to 30 years for standard asphalt shingles, while premium materials like metal, tile, or slate can last 40 to 100+ years"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Utah's extreme weather\u2014heavy winter snow loads, ice dams, high-altitude UV rays, and hot summers\u2014can wear down materials faster than in milder regions.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Roof Lifespan by Material in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "3-Tab Asphalt Shingles: 15\u201320 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Architectural Asphalt Shingles: 18\u201330 years (the Utah standard for most homes)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: 40\u201370 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Concrete or Clay Tile: 40\u201360+ years (up to 100 years with proper care)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Slate Roofing: 75\u2013100+ years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Synthetic / Composite Roofing: 30\u201350 years"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Flat/Low-Slope (EPDM, TPO, PVC): 20\u201335 years",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3,
              4,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How Utah\u2019s Climate Impacts Your Roof"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Heavy Snow & Ice Dams: Accumulating snow puts structural weight on the roof, and melting/refreezing cycles create ice dams that lift shingles and force water underneath."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Intense UV Exposure: High elevation in the Mountain West means stronger ultraviolet radiation, which dries out, curls, and degrades asphalt shingles prematurely.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Thermal Shock: Rapid temperature swings\u2014going from freezing winter nights to warm daytime sun\u2014cause building materials to expand and contract repeatedly."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Poor Ventilation & Attic Heat: Trapped heat and moisture in the attic during Utah's hot summers can cook shingles from the underside and rot roof decking.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Learn more about evaluating options through the Reimagine Roofing Utah Guide . Regular inspections and proper attic ventilation can add 5 to 10 years to your roof's expected life.",
